RozeLynx pam-passkeys: browser-side prompts for the PAM platform
authenticator.

The authenticator fires the regular "webauthn-prompt" observer JSON with
three new prompt types while a PAM verification runs:
- "rozelynx-pam-verify": a doorhanger ("look at the camera or wait for the
  password prompt") with a cancel button, shown while howdy grabs the camera;
- "rozelynx-pam-password": the PAM conversation asked for a secret - a
  password dialog (promptPasswordBC) whose answer goes back through
  nsIWebAuthnService::pinCallback, cancel through ::cancel;
- "rozelynx-pam-select-authenticator": registration with an open attachment
  asks where to save the passkey: this device (face/password) or a USB
  security key; the choice arrives through ::selectionCallback.

The "cancel" prompt type (already handled) clears the doorhangers when the
PAM transaction finishes.

